TEXT -144 -48 Left 2 !.param tdv=1 tdt=1 fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1} length=10 PN=200e6 QN=50e6
TEXT -288 0 Left 2 !.options vntol=1m abstol=1u reltol=0.01
TEXT -160 -104 Left 2 ;distributed
TEXT 280 -160 Left 2 ;3polig 1.2kA phase and 690A sheath Z=270-7j
TEXT -288 16 Left 2 !.tran 0 200m 0 0.1m
TEXT -160 424 Left 2 ;distributed
TEXT 272 352 Left 2 ;3polig 1.2kA phase and no Sheath current zero Z=270-7j Voltage at open end U=1kV (100V for 1km cable length )\nThe sheath voltage is always halved by doubling the count of sections !!
TEXT 272 496 Left 2 ;With no side grounding the sheath current is zerod\nand the compensating of Xphase is also zero\nTherefore Xphase will be the highest and\nso the Phase current is smallest\nThe disadvantage is that the sheath voltage\nis relative high
TEXT 272 320 Left 5 ;Sectionized single point grounding (eg. each 500m)
TEXT 296 -240 Left 5 ;Sectionized two point grounding\nPhase configuration horizontal
TEXT 336 -32 Left 2 ;With two point grounding the sheath current is highest\nsame as the phase current and so the compensation effect\nof Xphase is maximal. The current in the phase is \nalso maximal.
TEXT -8 0 Left 5 ;Linelength=10km
TEXT 296 -200 Left 2 ;NOTE: For short lines (1km) sheaths current much lower then by the 10km example here!!!\nFor sectionizing in 3 sections the current decrease from 1kA to 690A wich is not the halve
TEXT 640 -160 Left 2 ;3x200MW+j50MW
TEXT 656 360 Left 2 ;3x200MW+j50MW
TEXT -160 168 Left 2 ;distributed
TEXT 280 112 Left 2 ;3polig 1.2kA phase and 300A sheath Z=270-7j
TEXT 296 32 Left 5 ;Sectionized two point grounding with more sections\nPhase configuration horizontal
TEXT 272 256 Left 2 ;With two point grounding the sheath current is highest\nsame as the phase current and so the compensation effect\nof Xphase is maximal. The current in the phase is \nalso maximal.
TEXT 696 112 Left 2 ;3polig 1.2kA phase and 300A sheath Z=255+55j
TEXT 1504 112 Left 2 ;3x200MW+j50MW
TEXT 1112 112 Left 2 ;3polig 1.2kA phase and 690A sheath Z=255+55j
TEXT 832 8 Left 2 ;You see that the sheath with the 9 section current is not\n1/3 of the current of the 3 section example (690A vs 300A) \nand not 1/10 of the current of the 1 section example (1kA vs 300A)\nThis is true because the sheats impedance is always dependent\nof the length and smaller sheats impedance means higher\nsheats currents. Therefore the sectionizing of the two point\ngrounding method is not appropriate. More sense makes \nsectionizing the single point grounding method
TEXT 296 72 Left 2 ;NOTE: For short lines (1km) sheaths current much lower then by the 10km example here!!!\nFor sectionizing in 9 sections the current decrease from 1kA to 300A wich is not 1/9
TEXT -32 -264 Left 2 ;NOTE:\nQ is not 150e6 of the load\nbecause the cable capacitance\nis high (about 170MVAr for 10km length)\nYou see this also by measuring\nthe reactance X wich is negativ !
